<script type="application/ld+json" id="glowth-page-faq">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Does my Abu Dhabi clinic need approval before running ads?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For medical and aesthetic services, generally yes. The Department of Health – Abu Dhabi regulates advertising of health products and services in the emirate and issues the permits. Medical product promotions also need prior MOHAP approval. We plan approval time into every launch. For your exact case, check the current DoH requirements on TAMM."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Should my salon's ads and Google profile be in Arabic, English, or both?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"For most Abu Dhabi businesses, both. Arabic and English searchers use different words, so a translated ad usually performs worse than one written natively. We run separate Arabic and English ad groups and keep your Google Business Profile, website and review replies bilingual."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can one campaign cover Abu Dhabi city and Al Ain?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We don't recommend it. Al Ain is a separate city of around a million people (SCAD, 2024), with its own municipality and a long drive from the capital. A shared campaign usually spends money in the area where you have no branch. If you have branches in both, each gets its own location targeting, Google profile and budget."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who inspects beauty salons and barbershops in Abu Dhabi?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The municipalities under the Department of Municipalities and Transport: Abu Dhabi City Municipality and Al Ain City Municipality, through their public health teams. They run regular hygiene inspection campaigns, often before Eid. Medical-grade treatments are a different matter and fall under the DoH."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is men's grooming worth a separate marketing budget here?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often, yes. SCAD reports Abu Dhabi's population is about 67% male. In Al Ain, the municipality counted 791 men's beauty centres out of 1,190 in 2024. If you serve men, they need their own creative, offers and audiences, not a footnote in a ladies' campaign."}}]}</script>
