          <dl class="lp-area__facts">
                        <div><dt>Where we start (Glowth view)</dt><dd>Maps + Instagram</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Radius we&apos;d test</dt><dd>The island itself</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Watch-out</dt><dd>Many new openings</dd></div>
                      </dl>
        </div>
                <div class="lp-area" role="tabpanel" id="lp-area-khalidiya" aria-labelledby="lp-tab-khalidiya" hidden>
          <div class="lp-area__copy">
            <h3>Khalidiya &amp; Al Zahiyah</h3>
            <p>Old, central neighbourhoods with long-running salons and loyal clients. Many of those clients book through word of mouth and WhatsApp. Arabic review replies and a complete, up-to-date Google profile usually matter more here than a flashy ad.</p>
            <ul class="lp-tags">
              <li>Established central areas</li><li>Repeat clients</li><li>WhatsApp booking culture</li>            </ul>
          </div>
          <dl class="lp-area__facts">
                        <div><dt>Where we start (Glowth view)</dt><dd>Reviews + Local SEO</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Language mix</dt><dd>Arabic &amp; English</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Watch-out</dt><dd>Parking-led search</dd></div>
                      </dl>
        </div>
                <div class="lp-area" role="tabpanel" id="lp-area-bateen" aria-labelledby="lp-tab-bateen" hidden>
          <div class="lp-area__copy">
            <h3>Al Bateen</h3>
            <p>A quieter, villa-heavy and well-established part of the island. Clients here value discretion and trust. For a dermatology or aesthetic clinic, that means a careful, claim-safe website and appointment-only messaging. Discount-led ads tend to work against you.</p>
            <ul class="lp-tags">
              <li>Villas &amp; residences</li><li>Discretion valued</li><li>Premium clinics</li>            </ul>
          </div>
          <dl class="lp-area__facts">
                        <div><dt>Where we start (Glowth view)</dt><dd>Search + website</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Tone</dt><dd>Understated, bilingual</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Watch-out</dt><dd>DoH ad approval</dd></div>
                      </dl>
        </div>
                <div class="lp-area" role="tabpanel" id="lp-area-yas" aria-labelledby="lp-tab-yas" hidden>
          <div class="lp-area__copy">
            <h3>Yas &amp; Saadiyat Islands</h3>
            <p>These are Abu Dhabi's leisure and culture islands: Yas has Yas Marina Circuit, Yas Mall and Etihad Arena, and Saadiyat has the Louvre Abu Dhabi and its beach resorts. Residents book like locals, but on event weekends demand rises from hotel guests. We raise budgets around those dates rather than spending flat all year.</p>
            <ul class="lp-tags">
              <li>Residents + hotel guests</li><li>Event-driven peaks</li><li>Mobile “near me” search</li>            </ul>
          </div>
          <dl class="lp-area__facts">
                        <div><dt>Where we start (Glowth view)</dt><dd>Google Ads + Maps</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Timing</dt><dd>Event calendar</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Watch-out</dt><dd>Hotel spas compete</dd></div>
                      </dl>
        </div>
                <div class="lp-area" role="tabpanel" id="lp-area-khalifa" aria-labelledby="lp-tab-khalifa" hidden>
          <div class="lp-area__copy">
            <h3>Khalifa City &amp; Al Raha</h3>
            <p>Mainland family suburbs between the airport and the islands. Many residents would rather not drive onto the island for a blow-dry or a facial. A salon that ranks well locally on the mainland can win them over. Home-service and ladies-only offers are worth testing here.</p>
            <ul class="lp-tags">
              <li>Family villas</li><li>Avoid the island commute</li><li>Ladies-only demand</li>            </ul>
          </div>
          <dl class="lp-area__facts">
                        <div><dt>Where we start (Glowth view)</dt><dd>Local SEO</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Language mix</dt><dd>Strong Arabic share</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Watch-out</dt><dd>Wide catchment</dd></div>
                      </dl>
        </div>
                <div class="lp-area" role="tabpanel" id="lp-area-alain" aria-labelledby="lp-tab-alain" hidden>
          <div class="lp-area__copy">
            <h3>Al Ain</h3>
            <p>The emirate's second city, with around a million people in the Al Ain region according to SCAD. It has its own municipality and is a long drive from the capital. Al Ain City Municipality counted 1,190 beauty centres in 2024, and 791 of them serve men. Al Ain needs its own campaigns, its own Google profile and Arabic-first creative. It should not be a corner of an Abu Dhabi city budget.</p>
            <ul class="lp-tags">
              <li>Separate city, separate budget</li><li>Arabic-first</li><li>Large men&apos;s grooming market</li>            </ul>
          </div>
          <dl class="lp-area__facts">
                        <div><dt>Where we start (Glowth view)</dt><dd>Arabic search + Maps</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Regulator for salons</dt><dd>Al Ain City Municipality</dd></div>
                        <div><dt>Watch-out</dt><dd>Don&apos;t target the whole emirate</dd></div>
                      </dl>
        </div>
              </div>
      <p class="lp-note lp-note--dark">Al Ain figures: <a href="https://dmt.gov.ae/en/aam/Media-Centre/News/Al-Ain-City-Municipality-organizes-the-Health-and-Beauty-Forum" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#C6F432;text-decoration:underline">Al Ain City Municipality, Jul 2024</a> · <a href="https://scad.gov.ae/w/abu-dhabi-population-in-2024-grows-7-5-to-reach-4-14m" target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="color:#C6F432;text-decoration:underline">SCAD 2024</a>. All other notes are Glowth's planning view.</p>
      <div class="lp-center">
        <a href="/get-a-free-audit/" class="lp-btn lp-btn--grad">Book My Abu Dhabi Audit<svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a>      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="lp-section lp-section--soft" id="rules">
    <div class="lp-wrap">
      <div class="lp-head lp-head--center"><span class="lp-kicker">Who regulates what in Abu Dhabi</span><h2 class="lp-title">Clinics answer to the DoH. <span class="hl">Salons answer to the municipality.</span></h2><p class="lp-intro">Clinics and salons in Abu Dhabi report to different authorities, so a marketing plan has to start with knowing which rules apply to you. This is how we read it. It is not legal advice, so confirm your own case with the authority.</p></div>      <div class="lp-rules lp-rules--2">
                <article class="lp-rule">
          <span class="lp-rule__tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5.5c0 4.4-3 8.2-7 9.5-4-1.3-7-5.1-7-9.5V6z"/><path d="M8.8 12.2l2.2 2.2 4.2-4.4"/></svg>Clinics, medspas, dermatology</span>
          <h3>Department of Health – Abu Dhabi (DoH)</h3>
          <div class="lp-rule__body"><p>The DoH is the emirate's healthcare regulator. It licenses healthcare facilities and the professionals who work in them, and it also regulates advertising of health products and services in Abu Dhabi and issues the permits for it. In Dubai, the DHA does that job. Approval for an Abu Dhabi clinic ad comes from the DoH, and promotions for medical products also need prior approval from the federal Ministry of Health and Prevention (MOHAP).</p><p>What this means for your marketing:</p><ul><li>Treat every ad, boosted post and promo for a medical or aesthetic service as health advertising. Plan time for DoH approval before launch. TAMM lists DoH services to log and re-log a health advertisement.</li><li>Keep claims something you can prove. Leave out “guaranteed results” and “no side effects” style wording.</li><li>Make sure the treatments you promote match your facility licence and your practitioners' DoH licences.</li></ul><small>Sources: <a href="https://www.ibanet.org/document?id=Healthcare-Survey-Responses-2024-United-Arab-Emirates" target="_blank" rel="noopener">IBA Healthcare Survey 2024 – UAE</a> · <a href="https://www.tamimi.com/law-update-articles/termination-of-general-clinic-licences-in-abu-dhabi-implementation-of-new-primary-healthcare-centre-licence/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Al Tamimi – DoH facility licensing</a> · <a href="https://www.tamm.abudhabi/en/life-events/business/Manage-your-Business/Advertisement/RequestforHealthAdvertisement" target="_blank" rel="noopener">TAMM – Request to Log a Health Advertisement</a></small></div>
        </article>
                <article class="lp-rule">
          <span class="lp-rule__tag"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 3l7 3v5.5c0 4.4-3 8.2-7 9.5-4-1.3-7-5.1-7-9.5V6z"/><path d="M8.8 12.2l2.2 2.2 4.2-4.4"/></svg>Salons, barbers, beauty centres</span>
          <h3>Abu Dhabi City Municipality &amp; Al Ain City Municipality (DMT)</h3>
          <div class="lp-rule__body"><p>Non-medical salons and beauty centres are inspected for public health and hygiene by the municipalities under the Department of Municipalities and Transport (DMT). In April 2024, Abu Dhabi City Municipality's Public Health Department ran more than 100 inspection visits on beauty centres, ladies' salons and barbershops before Eid Al-Fitr. A September 2025 campaign cited Law No. (2) of 2012 and its executive regulations. Al Ain City Municipality runs its own inspections and industry forums.</p><p>What this means for your marketing:</p><ul><li>Hygiene and sterilisation are what inspectors check, and clients notice them too. Show them in your content.</li><li>If you advertise laser, injectables or any medical-grade treatment, check first whether it falls under DoH rules.</li><li>Expect inspection campaigns before Eid, when salons are busiest. Book your peak-season ads around them.</li></ul><small>Sources: <a href="https://www.dmt.gov.ae/en/adm/Media-Centre/News/03Apr2024" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DMT, 3 Apr 2024</a> · <a href="https://www.dmt.gov.ae/en/adm/Media-Centre/News/17Sep2025" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DMT, 17 Sep 2025</a> · <a href="https://dmt.gov.ae/en/aam/Media-Centre/News/Al-Ain-City-Municipality-organizes-the-Health-and-Beauty-Forum" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Al Ain City Municipality, Jul 2024</a></small></div>
        </article>
              </div>
      <p class="lp-note">Our <a href="/clinic-marketing-uae-guide/">guide to compliant clinic marketing in the UAE</a> covers claims, before-and-after content and platform policies. If you run a clinic, see how we work with <a href="/aesthetic-clinics/">aesthetic clinics</a> and <a href="/dermatology-clinics/">dermatology practices</a>.</p>    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="lp-section">
    <div class="lp-wrap lp-maps">
      <div class="lp-head"><span class="lp-kicker">Local SEO, in two languages</span><h2 class="lp-title">Show up on the map <span class="hl">whichever language she searches in</span></h2><p class="lp-intro">Many Abu Dhabi clients search Google Maps in Arabic. If your Google Business Profile only has English categories, services and replies, you are much less visible to them. We build the profile, services list and review replies in both languages.</p></div>      <figure class="lp-map">
